---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import DockerGetStarted from '../components/DockerGetStarted.astro'
import DockerDownload from '../components/DockerDownload.astro'
import data from '../data/releases.json'
import desktop from '../data/desktop.json'
import { humanSize } from '../lib/releases.js'

const [latest, ...older] = data.releases
// The Windows installer leads once a release of it exists; until then the page is the Docker install's, as before.
const win = desktop.releases[0] ?? null
const winDate = win && new Date(win.publishedAt).toLocaleDateString('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' })
// The demo videos are switched off for now (they took too long to rebuild on every release): see README, "Demo videos".
---
<Base>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Degree planning, kept private</p>
      <h1>Map your whole degree.<br />Keep your data to yourself.</h1>
      <p class="lede">MyDegreePlan lays out every semester, checks prerequisites for you, and runs entirely on your own computer, so no one else ever sees your plan.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        {win
          ? <a class="btn" href={win.installer.url}>Download for Windows</a>
          : latest
            ? <a class="btn" href={latest.zip.url}>Download v{latest.version}</a>
            : <a class="btn" aria-disabled="true" href="#download">First release coming soon</a>}
        <a class="btn ghost" href="#features">What it does</a>
      </div>
      {win
        ? <p class="small">Free. Windows 10 or 11, nothing else to install. On Mac or Linux, use the <a href="#download">Docker install</a>.</p>
        : <p class="small">Free. Needs Docker Desktop. Windows is the most thoroughly tested; Mac and Linux launchers are included.</p>}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="features">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What it does</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card"><h3>Semester-by-semester grid</h3><p>See every course you still need, laid out across your remaining semesters.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Prerequisite checking</h3><p>Get warned when a course is planned before its prerequisites or corequisites are met.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Concentrations</h3><p>Core, Cybersecurity, Data Science &amp; AI, and High Performance Computing plans built in.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Prior credit wizard</h3><p>Enter AP, IB, and transfer credit; covered courses drop off your plan automatically.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Drag and drop</h3><p>Move courses between semesters and see the effect immediately.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Progress tracking</h3><p>Mark semesters complete and watch your completion and credit totals update.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="privacy">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Private by design</h2>
      <p class="lede">Your plan lives on your own disk. There is no account with us and no server holding your data.</p>
      <div class="grid">
        {win ? (
          <>
            <div class="card"><h3>Only you can open it</h3><p>The app opens its own window and listens on no network port, so nothing on your Wi-Fi can reach it.</p></div>
            <div class="card"><h3>No third parties</h3><p>Opening the planner contacts no analytics, fonts, or ad services, and the app window is blocked from connecting anywhere else.</p></div>
            <div class="card"><h3>One small outbound check</h3><p>To offer updates, the app asks GitHub whether a newer version exists. Nothing about you or your plan is sent.</p></div>
          </>
        ) : (
          <>
            <div class="card"><h3>Only you can open it</h3><p>The app listens on your computer only, not on your Wi-Fi network.</p></div>
            <div class="card"><h3>No third parties</h3><p>Opening the planner contacts no analytics, fonts, or ad services.</p></div>
            <div class="card"><h3>One small outbound check</h3><p>To offer updates, the app asks GitHub for a ~1 KB version file. Nothing about you or your plan is sent, and you can turn it off.</p></div>
          </>
        )}
      </div>
      {win
        ? <p class="small">Your plan is stored in your Windows user profile. Protect the laptop itself with a login password and disk encryption (BitLocker), and use Export in Settings to keep a backup copy.</p>
        : <p class="small">Protect the laptop itself with a login password and disk encryption (BitLocker or FileVault). Backups and the <code>.env</code> file are not encrypted.</p>}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="get-started">
    <div class="wrap">
      {win ? (
        <>
          <h2>Get started in three steps</h2>
          <ol class="steps">
            <li><strong>Download the installer.</strong> <a href={win.installer.url}>MyDegreePlan-Setup.exe</a> ({humanSize(win.installer.size)}).</li>
            <li><strong>Run it.</strong> It installs for your account only and needs no administrator rights. If Windows says "Windows protected your PC", that is because the installer is not code-signed yet: choose <strong>More info</strong>, then <strong>Run anyway</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>Open MyDegreePlan.</strong> It starts when the install finishes, and later from the Start menu. Choose your program and start planning. There is no account to create.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="small">New versions arrive through a card inside the app. You choose when to download and when to restart, and your plan is kept.</p>
          <details style="margin-top:20px">
            <summary>Mac, Linux, or you prefer Docker</summary>
            <p class="small">The Docker install runs the same planner in containers. It is the way to use MyDegreePlan on Mac and Linux.</p>
            <DockerGetStarted />
          </details>
        </>
      ) : (
        <>
          <h2>Get started in three steps</h2>
          <DockerGetStarted />
        </>
      )}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="download">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Download</h2>
      {win ? (
        <>
          <p class="lede">Version <strong>{win.version}</strong> · {winDate}</p>
          <div class="actions"><a class="btn" href={win.installer.url}>Download MyDegreePlan-Setup.exe ({humanSize(win.installer.size)})</a></div>
          <p class="small">Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit.</p>
          {win.notes && <details open><summary>What's new</summary><p class="notes">{win.notes}</p></details>}
          <details>
            <summary>Verify your download</summary>
            {win.installer.sha256 && <dl class="meta"><dt>SHA-256</dt><dd><code>{win.installer.sha256}</code></dd></dl>}
            <p class="small">In PowerShell: <code>Get-FileHash MyDegreePlan-Setup.exe</code>. The installer is not code-signed yet, so this checks that the file you got is the one published.</p>
          </details>
          <p class="small">Older versions are listed in the <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '')}/changelog`}>changelog</a>.</p>
          <details style="margin-top:20px">
            <summary>Mac, Linux, or the Docker install</summary>
            <DockerDownload latest={latest} olderCount={older.length} />
          </details>
        </>
      ) : (
        <DockerDownload latest={latest} olderCount={older.length} />
      )}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="faq">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <details><summary>Do I need to be online?</summary><p>Only to download it and to get updates. Planning works fully offline once it is running.</p></details>
      {win && (
        <>
          <details><summary>Why does Windows warn me when I run the installer?</summary><p>The installer is not code-signed yet, so Windows SmartScreen does not recognize the publisher. Choose <strong>More info</strong>, then <strong>Run anyway</strong>. You can compare the file's SHA-256 with the one listed under Download first.</p></details>
          <details><summary>How do I move to a new computer?</summary><p>In the app, open Settings and choose <strong>Export</strong> to save a backup file. On the new computer, install MyDegreePlan and choose <strong>Import</strong> on the first screen, or in Settings.</p></details>
          <details><summary>How do I uninstall it?</summary><p>Windows Settings, then Apps, then MyDegreePlan, then Uninstall. Your plan is kept so a reinstall finds it. To remove it too, choose <strong>Erase</strong> in the app's Settings before you uninstall.</p></details>
        </>
      )}
      {win ? (
        <details>
          <summary>Docker install questions</summary>
          <details><summary>The launcher says ".env is missing but a database already exists"</summary><p>You started from a folder that doesn't have the original <code>.env</code> file, and this computer already holds a plan. Copy the <code>.env</code> from your original MyDegreePlan folder into this one. Do <strong>not</strong> run <code>mdp wipe</code> unless you want to permanently delete your plan.</p></details>
          <details><summary>What if I forget my password?</summary><p>There is no reset email. Run <code>mdp reset-password your@email</code> from the folder to set a new one.</p></details>
          <details><summary>How do I move to a new computer?</summary><p>Run <code>mdp backup</code> to create a file in <code>backups/</code>, copy that folder and your <code>.env</code> file over, then run <code>mdp restore</code>.</p></details>
        </details>
      ) : (
        <>
          <details><summary>The launcher says ".env is missing but a database already exists"</summary><p>You started from a folder that doesn't have the original <code>.env</code> file, and this computer already holds a plan. Copy the <code>.env</code> from your original MyDegreePlan folder into this one. Do <strong>not</strong> run <code>mdp wipe</code> unless you want to permanently delete your plan.</p></details>
          <details><summary>What if I forget my password?</summary><p>There is no reset email. Run <code>mdp reset-password your@email</code> from the folder to set a new one.</p></details>
          <details><summary>How do I move to a new computer?</summary><p>Run <code>mdp backup</code> to create a file in <code>backups/</code>, copy that folder and your <code>.env</code> file over, then run <code>mdp restore</code>.</p></details>
        </>
      )}
      <details><summary>Is this an official registration or advising tool?</summary><p>No. It is a planning aid. Always confirm requirements with your academic advisor.</p></details>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
